2,"Manobo, Ata Language (ATD) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/atd/,"Ata Manobo is a stable indigenous language of the Philippines. It belongs to the Austronesian language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.","Manobo, Ata",Austronesian
3,Ata Manobo - atd (Austronesian) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/atd/,"Ata Manobo (atd) is part of the Austronesian family and Austronesian, Malayo-Polynesian, Greater Central Philippine, Manobo, Central, South, Ata-Tigwa class. Ata Manobo speaking People Groups across the world: Fast Facts","Manobo, Ata",Austronesian
4,Ata Manobo language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/ata_manobo_language,"The Ata Manobo language has a consonant inventory of 16 phonemes, typical of many Manobo languages within the Austronesian family.","Manobo, Ata",Austronesian
